---
import { BUSINESS } from '../config.ts';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const mail = `mailto:${BUSINESS.email}`;
---

<Base title="Terms of use" description="The terms for using SolLock, the non-custodial time lock for your own Solana.">
  <h1 class="section-title">Terms of use</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      {BUSINESS.tradeName} (sollock.io) is a sole trader in {BUSINESS.place}{BUSINESS.kvk && `, registered with the Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK) under number ${BUSINESS.kvk}`}{BUSINESS.vat && `, VAT number ${BUSINESS.vat}`}.
      You can reach us at <a href={mail}>{BUSINESS.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What SolLock does</h2>
    <p>
      SolLock is software that runs in your browser. It builds a Solana transaction that creates a stake account with a lockup: an
      account holding your Solana that the Solana network will not let anyone withdraw from before the date you choose. You check that
      transaction and sign it in your own wallet. The Solana network then keeps the lock. The lock's custodian is an address that
      nobody has a key for, so nobody, including you and us, can lift the lock early.
    </p>
    <p>
      We never hold, receive or control your crypto or your keys, and we never sign anything for you. We keep no accounts and store no
      data about you or your locks.
    </p>

    <h2>3. What SolLock does not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We do not look after your crypto. We are not a bank, an exchange or a custodian.</li>
      <li>We give no financial, investment, legal or tax advice, and we never predict prices.</li>
      <li>A lock pays no interest or other return.</li>
      <li>We cannot unlock a lock early, for any reason, and we cannot recover a lost wallet or recovery phrase.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Fee</h2>
    <p>
      For each lock we charge 0.25% of the amount you lock, at least 0.01 SOL, including VAT. The fee is paid in
      SOL, in the same transaction that creates the lock, and the preview shows it before you sign. Test locks of exactly 0.01 SOL that
      open within about a day are free. The Solana network fee and the rent deposit are not ours: the network fee goes to Solana, and
      the rent deposit stays in your lock and comes back when you withdraw.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Right of withdrawal</h2>
    <p>
      As a consumer in the EU you normally have 14 days to withdraw from a contract made online. Our service is performed in full the
      moment your lock is created, and a lock cannot be undone. Before you sign, you ask us to perform the service straight away and
      confirm that you lose your right of withdrawal once the lock is created.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Your part</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Keep your wallet's recovery phrase safe and offline. Never share it. We will never ask for it.</li>
      <li>Check the transaction in your wallet before you sign. Only sign what you understand.</li>
      <li>For a gift, use the address of a self-custody wallet the recipient controls, never an exchange deposit address.</li>
      <li>Do not use SolLock for anything illegal, such as hiding money from creditors, money laundering or avoiding sanctions.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Risks</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>If you, or the recipient of a gift, lose the wallet's recovery phrase, the Solana in the lock is lost for good.</li>
      <li>The price of Solana can fall while it is locked, and you cannot sell it until the date.</li>
      <li>Solana is run by others. Its software can change or have faults, and it can be slow or unavailable at times.</li>
      <li>Wallet apps change over the years. You may need different software to withdraw on the date.</li>
      <li>The network's clock can run a little behind real time, so a lock may open slightly after the moment you picked.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>8. Liability</h2>
    <p>
      We build SolLock with care and test it thoroughly, but we cannot promise it is free of faults. As far as the law allows, we are
      not liable for losses that come from the risks in section 7, from the Solana network, from your wallet software, or from you
      signing a transaction. Our liability for any lock is limited to the fee you paid us for it. This does not limit our liability for
      intent or gross negligence, or any right you have under mandatory consumer law.
    </p>

    <h2>9. If SolLock stops</h2>
    <p>
      The website may change or go away. Your locks do not depend on it: they are ordinary Solana stake accounts, and after the date you
      can withdraw with any tool that supports stake accounts. The recovery note explains how.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may change these terms. The version on this page when you create a lock applies to that lock. This version is dated 3 November 2026.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Law and complaints</h2>
    <p>
      Dutch law applies. If you live in another EU country, you keep the protection of the mandatory consumer law of that country.
      Disputes go to the competent court in Rotterdam, unless the law gives you the right to go to the court where you live. If you
      have a complaint, write to <a href={mail}>{BUSINESS.email}</a> and we will answer within 14 days.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
